-- Records when each comissão permanente was created.
--
-- Not a legislaturaId, which is what the plan first assumed. A permanent committee does not
-- belong to a term: none of the thirty has a dataFim, and they carry on across mandates. What
-- they do have is a start, and five of them only started on 2023-02-15 — the opening of the
-- 57th — so showing those five while an earlier term is selected is the same kind of wrong
-- the propositions had.
--
-- Nullable because the list endpoint does not return it. It is filled in from the detail of
-- each committee, and a row with no date yet is shown rather than hidden: not knowing when
-- something started is not evidence that it had not.
--
-- A plain ALTER, unlike the previous two migrations: the existing columns are untouched and
-- nothing stored has to be thrown away.
ALTER TABLE Orgao ADD COLUMN dataInicio TEXT;
